# Model-Aware Prompt Enhancer configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis and enhancement need NO API keys and make NO network calls.
# The tool does not read .env files itself. Export variables in your shell
# (for example: set -a; source .env; set +a) or set them in your harness config.
# NEVER commit your real '.env' file.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default model id when --model is not passed (e.g. claude-sonnet-5, gpt-4.1, o3, gemini-3-pro, or claude/gpt/gemini)
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# No structural changes for prompts shorter than this many words (default 8; diagnostics still run)
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_MIN_WORDS=8

# Approximate token count at which a prompt counts as long context (default 4000)
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_LONG_CONTEXT_TOKENS=4000

# Comma-separated rule ids to turn off, e.g. PE102,PE503
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_DISABLE_RULES=

# Extra profile directory containing models/*.json (and optionally harnesses/harnesses.json)
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_PROFILES_DIR=./my-profiles

# Where `prompt-enhancer sources check` stores documentation fingerprints (default ~/.cache/prompt-enhancer)
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_CACHE_DIR=~/.cache/prompt-enhancer

# --- Optional: only for `prompt-enhancer eval-e2e` (sends prompts to the provider and costs money) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# --- Optional: Claude Code hook (experimental) ---
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_DISABLE=0            # set to 1 to switch the hook off
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_SHOW_SUGGESTIONS=1   # set to 0 to hide warnings in the transcript
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_RESTATE=0            # set to 1 to also restate your constraints to Claude as hidden context

# --- Optional: end-to-end A/B through your Claude Code login (no API key; uses your plan's usage) ---
# PROMPT_ENHANCER_CLAUDE_BIN=/path/to/claude   # defaults to `claude` on PATH
